{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791568859,"nonce":"0NCk6ilCbvxNOlNka2718iuDGTE=","title":"Window frame waits time out intermittently in local macOS native runs","message":"On 2026-10-09, three local runs on the macOS desktop failed on a wait for a window frame, and each test passed on rerun: native-host.mjs (\"First mounted frame\", once, standalone) and native-scene-window.mjs (\"Replacement scene frame\", twice in a full npm run test:native, with no failure in eight standalone or paired reruns, nor in two more full runs with diagnostics). Linux CI (x11 and wayland) passed on the same commits.\n\nNot yet known whether this is new with the command buffer (ede8ea0) or was already there, since the earlier full runs happened to pass. The waits require host.frames to advance within 5 s after attaching a scene; a frame that is never requested, or a window the system reports occluded or hidden, would look the same.\n\n**Next**\nLog host.frames, stats, isVisible and isMinimized when a wait times out, and run the native suite in a loop on an idle desktop to get a rate before and after ede8ea0.","files":null}]}